course: dictionary
lesson: 249
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, so context tells you which one is meant. The word alpha is the first letter of the Greek alphabet, written Α or α. The word alphabet comes from alpha and beta, the first two Greek letters.
explain: «The idea of an alpha wolf fighting its way to the top came from captive wolves; wild packs are mostly parents leading their family.» Here alpha means the top leader, the one who is first. The sentence also tells you this idea is now thought to be too simple.
explain: Read the clues around the word. In a computer lesson, an «alpha version» is an early test, not the finished game. In a spelling code, Alpha stands for the letter A. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence, then swap your meaning in to check it.
fact: Alpha is the first letter of the Greek alphabet, written Α or α.
fact: Alpha can mean first or top, as in the alpha wolf that leads the pack.
fact: An alpha version is an early, unfinished test version of a program or game.
fact: In everyday talk children are called «Gen Alpha».
fact: In the Bible, «The Alpha and the Omega» means the first and the last, the beginning and the end.
exercise: Which alphabet is alpha the first letter of? | Russian | Arabic | *Greek
exercise: «The alpha wolf leads the pack.» What does alpha mean here? | The first letter of the alphabet | *The first or top one | A wolf with a bad tail
exercise: What is an «alpha version» of a game? | The final version sold in shops | *An early, unfinished test version | A game for babies
test: In a spelling code, «Alpha» stands for which letter? | *A | C | Z | B
test: What does «The Alpha and the Omega» mean? | A type of computer game | *The beginning and the end | Two kinds of wolf
exam: Why does the word «alphabet» come from alpha and beta? | Because beta is the name of a wolf | Because both words mean the same thing | Because alpha is a fish | *Because alpha and beta are the first two Greek letters
